      {
        "caution_id": "evidence-gap:ac1683c6ceea935d59a7c46b",
        "description": "Individual-cell lineage tracing: Probabilistic temporal coupling is not direct physical tracing of the same cells.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "content_hash": "1e70ac685568c76b48611cd2b60e2c8304292e0fb5fcecd9a6b1aebbc2e428fa",
            "end_offset": 6483,
            "evidence_span_id": "evidence-span:02693d7a0ceded625a0e1b2f",
            "exact_text": "Our goal is to learn the relationship between ancestor cells at one time point and descendant cells at another time point:\ngiven that a cell has a specific expression profile at one time point, where will its descendants likely be at a later time point\nand where are its likely ancestors at an earlier time point? We model a differentiating population of cells as a time-varying\nprobability distribution (i.e., stochastic process) on a high-dimensional expression space. By sampling this\nprobability distribution ℙt at various time points t, we wish to infer how the\ndifferentiation process evolves over time (Figure 1A). From a large number of cells at a\ngiven time point (Figure 1B), we can approximate the distribution at that time point, but,\nbecause different cells are sampled independently at different time points, we lose the joint distribution of expression between\npairs of time points, called temporal coupling. Absent any constraint on cellular transitions, we cannot infer\nthe temporal coupling, but if we assume that cells move short distances over short time periods, then we can infer the temporal\ncoupling by using the mathematical technique of optimal transport (Figure 1A, Methods S1).",
            "locator": {
              "kind": "section",
              "value": "source-artifact:187dcb65d05e57fe38fef995535347c8/xml:/article/body/sec[2]/sec[1]/p[1];text-sha256:d6a2cf29928f35d3f40d00651bf08f7569284951953f1ae26654b213b56efb6a:5278:6483"
            },
            "ontology_version": "2.0.0-core-review.1",
            "schema_version": "sckg-ontology-core-5c-design-v1",
